v	1
th	DEMO	1	2026-11-15	demo r0.9	User Commands
sh	NAME
tx	demo - exercise every roffsub element
sh	SYNOPSIS
nf
tx	\fBdemo\fR [\fB-r\fR] [\fB-k\fR \fIlist\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
fi
sh	DESCRIPTION
tx	\fBdemo\fR
tx	reads each \fIfile\fR in turn, or the standard input when none is named, and writes the records it finds in the order chosen by the options.
tx	A space written as a backslash space, as in a\~b\~c, never breaks.
tx	Fonts may change mid word, as in \fBsrt\fR(1) and \fIfile\fR.txt.
pp
tx	A second paragraph follows the first after one blank line, and it is long enough to wrap at every width the reference outputs use, which is the point of it.
sh	OPTIONS
tp		\fB-r\fR
tx	reverse the emitted order.
tp		\fB-k\fR \fIlist\fR
tx	sort by the columns in \fIlist\fR, then the remaining columns in order.
tp		\fB--respect-blanks\fR
tx	treat each indented block as a unit; the tag is longer than the indent, so the body starts on the next line.
tp	4	\fB-x\fR
tx	a width of four sets the prevailing indent, which the next item keeps.
tp		\fB-o\fI file\fR
tx	write to \fIfile\fR instead of the standard output.
ss	Lists
ip		o
tx	bullets use the bullet character, shown as o on an ASCII terminal.
ip		o
tx	a second bullet item.
ip	4	1.
tx	a numbered item with its own width.
ip		2.
tx	a second numbered item.
ss	Nesting
pp
tx	Text before a nested block.
rs	
tx	Nested text sits one prevailing indent further in.
rs	3
tx	A deeper block, moved in by three cells.
re
tx	Back at the first level.
re
tx	Back at the section margin.
br
tx	After a line break, still the same paragraph.
sp	2
tx	After two blank lines.
sh	TABLE
ts	
tf	lb	lb
tf	l	l
tr	OPTION	MEANING
t_
tr	\fB-r\fR	reverse the order
tr	\fB-k\fR \fIKEY\fR	sort on \fIKEY\fR
te
pp
tx	A boxed table with a text block:
ts	box
tf	lb	lb	rb
tf	l	l	r
tr	NAME	DESCRIPTION	SIZE
t_
tr	alpha	a long description that has to wrap when the terminal is narrow, kept inside its column	12
tr	beta	short	3456
te
sh	EXAMPLES
nf
tx	demo -k5,3 file
tx	demo -r < input > output
fi
sh	SEE ALSO
tx	\fBsrt\fR(1),
tx	\fBroffsub\fR(7)
